WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.067
On this slide, we are focusing on simple confidence interval idea.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:08.777
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:14.947
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.187
A sample estimate is uncertain.

00:00:17.187 --> 00:00:24.042
A confidence interval communicates a range around the estimate under the assumptions of the method.

00:00:24.042 --> 00:00:28.507
Before clicking Run, predict the statistic or pattern you expect.

00:00:28.507 --> 00:00:30.787
After it runs, interpret the result in words.

00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:35.232
Then change one value and see whether the interpretation changes.

00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:39.442
Focus on meaning and limitations, not only the calculation.

00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:45.187
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:50.603
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
